{"post": {"ID": 596, "post_title": "AI Brand Visibility Tools for B2B: What They Track and How to Choose", "post_excerpt": "What AI brand visibility tools track, what they cannot do, what two stand-alone trackers cost, and a 10-point checklist and 14-day test for choosing one for a B2B team.", "post_author": "3", "post_date": "2026-11-12 09:55:00", "post_modified": "2026-11-15 06:32:35", "post_content_b64": ""}, "meta": {"rl_type": "guide", "rl_updated": "2026-11-15", "rl_answer": "An AI brand visibility tool runs a fixed list of buyer questions through AI tools such as ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity and records whether your brand is named, linked or described correctly. Good tools show full answers, sources and history. No tool can give a reliable rank inside AI answers, because answers change from run to run. Test by hand first, then buy on what you can verify.", "rl_takeaways": "Tools track mentions, citations, share of voice, sources, sentiment and history. Keep mentions and citations separate.\nAnswers change from run to run: SparkToro found less than a 1 in 100 chance of the same brand list twice, so look for a rate, not a rank.\nNo third-party tool sees inside Google. Use Search Console's Generative AI report as a free first signal.\nSurveys of B2B buyers disagree because each asks a different question: Forrester 94% use AI somewhere, Gartner 45% on a recent purchase, 6sense 26% to discover vendors.\nEntry plans start near $29 to $95 a month, but prompts, engines and markets decide the real cost.\nRun a 14-day test with the same prompts in every trial and compare each tool with a hand baseline.", "rl_faqs": "What is an AI brand visibility tool? | Software that runs a fixed list of buyer questions through AI tools such as ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google's AI Overviews on a schedule and records whether your brand is named, linked or described correctly, compared with competitors.\nWhat do AI visibility tools track? | Most report mentions, citations, share of voice, sources cited, sentiment and history. Ahrefs and Semrush both list mentions, citations and share of voice or a visibility score. Check that a tool keeps mentions and citations separate.\nHow much do AI visibility tools cost? | It varies. In November 2026, Peec AI listed $95, $245 and $495 a month for 50, 150 and 350 prompts, and Otterly listed $29, $189 and $489 a month. Both offer custom enterprise plans. Prompts, engines, markets and staff time decide the real cost.\nAre AI visibility scores accurate? | They are directional. SparkToro and Gumshoe found less than a 1 in 100 chance that ChatGPT or Google's AI would give the same list of brands twice for one prompt, so a score from one day is a snapshot. Look for repeated runs and a trend.\nDo I need a paid AI visibility tool? | Not to start. Test 20 to 30 buyer questions by hand, use Search Console's Generative AI report and the free Ahrefs and Semrush checkers. Buy software when your prompt list or markets outgrow a spreadsheet.\nCan an AI visibility tool show my rank in AI answers? | Some report a position, but the order of brands in AI answers is close to random, so it is not a reliable measure. Use the share of runs in which you appear instead.\nDo AI visibility tools fix problems automatically? | No. They show gaps. Someone still has to correct facts, write pages and earn mentions, so decide who owns that work before you buy.\nWhich AI engines should a B2B tool cover? | The ones your buyers use, on the plan you would buy. For most B2B teams that means ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and AI Mode, Perplexity and Gemini. Entry plans often cover only some engines, so check the plan.\nHow many B2B buyers use AI to research vendors? | It depends on the question asked. Forrester found 94% use AI somewhere in buying, Gartner 45% on a recent purchase, and 6sense 81% use an LLM in an evaluation but only 26% to discover vendors.\nHow do I test an AI visibility tool before buying? | Write 20 to 30 buyer prompts without your brand name, run a hand baseline, trial each tool with the same prompts and competitors, compare the tool with your baseline, open ten answers to confirm the sources are real, and score each tool on a fixed checklist.", "rl_sources": "Forrester: B2B Buyers Make Zero-Click Buying Number One (January 2026) | https://www.forrester.com/blogs/b2b_buyers_make_zero_click_buying_number_one/\nGartner: Survey Finds 69% of B2B Buyers Turn to Sales Reps to Validate AI-Generated Insights (May 2026) | https://www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2026-05-20-gartner-survey-finds-sixty-nine-percent-of-b-two-b-buyers-turn-to-sales-reps-to-validate-ai-generated-insights\n6sense: 2026 Global B2B Buyer Experience Report (November 2026) | https://6sense.com/news/6sense-research-finds-that-vendors-need-to-be-known-and-preferred-before-the-buying-journey-begins\nSparkToro and Gumshoe: AIs are highly inconsistent when recommending brands or products (January 2026) | https://sparktoro.com/blog/new-research-ais-are-highly-inconsistent-when-recommending-brands-or-products-marketers-should-take-care-when-tracking-ai-visibility/\nGoogle Search Central: Guide to optimizing for generative AI features on Google Search | https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/ai-optimization-guide\nAhrefs: AI Visibility Audit | https://ahrefs.com/blog/ai-visibility-audit/\nAhrefs: Free AI Visibility Checker | https://ahrefs.com/ai-visibility-checker\nSemrush: Free AI Search Visibility Checker | https://www.semrush.com/free-tools/ai-search-visibility-checker/\nPeec AI: Pricing (read November 2026) | https://peec.ai/pricing\nOtterly.AI: Pricing (read November 2026) | https://otterly.ai/pricing\nSearch Atlas: How to choose an AI visibility tracking tool | https://searchatlas.com/blog/choose-ai-visibility-tracking-tool/\nVisilay: How to choose an AI visibility tool, 10 criteria | https://www.visilay.com/blog/how-to-choose-ai-visibility-tool/", "rl_g_glossary": "Prompt | The question you type into an AI tool.\nMention | An answer that names your brand.\nCitation | An answer that links to a page of yours.\nShare of voice | Your brand mentions divided by all brand mentions in the test.\nProof of value | A short trial that checks a tool against your own hand test.\nEngine | An AI search product such as ChatGPT, Gemini or Perplexity.", "rl_g_cta_service": "services/seo-ai-search-audit", "rl_g_cta_head": "Want the test done for you, with a written plan?", "rl_g_cta_sub": "Reinforce Lab starts with a free diagnostic of your Google and AI search visibility and a 90-day plan.", "rl_g_cta_button": "See the AI search audit", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "AI Brand Visibility Tools: How to Choose | Reinforce Lab", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "What AI brand visibility tools track, what they cannot do, what they cost and how to choose one for a B2B team, with a 14-day test and examples.", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "ai brand visibility tools", "_thumbnail_id": "597"}}